From 6bf2d72db2ca3165cf9cfe6bcd183cf0faaf5bba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port <port@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:09:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] dt-bindings: iommu: arm,smmu: add SM6225 Adreno SMMU

Add qcom,sm6225-smmu-500 to the SMMU-500 compatible lists (the
generic list and the Adreno list) and to the Adreno clock-name
constraint shared with QCM2290, SM6115 and SM6125
("mem", "hlos", "iface").

The Khaje Adreno SMMU matches the SM6115 one in the shipping
device tree: same base address (0x59a0000), same interrupt
layout (global SPI 163, contexts 167-174) and the same three
clocks. No driver change is needed: the generic qcom,smmu-500
match entry already selects the impl0 data, and the driver
explicitly asks not to grow the per-SoC match list for parts
covered by it. This only gives the node a SoC-specific
compatible to describe the hardware, instead of describing
Khaje silicon as another SoC.

Compile-tested only (schema); not verified on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Port <port@local>
